# H2 raw Android reference-device transcript

**Date:** 2026-11-10
**Branch:** `feat/mail-providers` (H2 review fixes on top of `da2cb29`)
**Device:** attached reference device `6bfcc911` (iPlay60 mini Turbo, `U812`)
**Android:** 14 / API 34, `arm64-v8a`, build type `user`
**Device state at capture:** USB powered, battery 100%, status full (5), 24.0 °C
**Runner:** native aarch64 test binary built from
`rust/pige_core/tests/recipient_perf.rs`; sha256
`b67101c105387dbb26481a510dae39a781df54f94315d37ef355acc55427e8aa`
**Host:** Fedora Linux x86_64; NDK `28.2.13676358`; release profile

This is the exact sanitized transcript behind the device numbers in
[`provider-performance.md`](provider-performance.md). The runner uses a
temporary SQLite file under `/data/local/tmp`; it never opens the Pige app
data, the user's real mail, or a provider account. Every fixture address is
synthetic `example.com`; no account, credential, key, message body, contact
payload, or real suggestion query appears in this log.

## Build

```console
$ export ANDROID_HOME="$HOME/Android/Sdk"
$ export ANDROID_NDK_HOME="$ANDROID_HOME/ndk/28.2.13676358"
$ TOOLCHAIN="$ANDROID_NDK_HOME/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64/bin"
$ export CARGO_TARGET_AARCH64_LINUX_ANDROID_LINKER="$TOOLCHAIN/aarch64-linux-android34-clang"
$ export CC_aarch64_linux_android="$CARGO_TARGET_AARCH64_LINUX_ANDROID_LINKER"
$ export CARGO_TARGET_AARCH64_LINUX_ANDROID_RUSTFLAGS="-C link-arg=-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384"
$ cd rust
$ cargo test --release --target aarch64-linux-android -p pige_core --test recipient_perf --no-run
   Compiling libsqlite3-sys v0.39.1
   Compiling rusqlite v0.41.1
   Compiling pige_core v2026.11.5 (/home/bronson/Projects/pige/rust/pige_core)
